The reviewer evidence points past the original cancellation test to a second, real production lifecycle bug: an automatic keepalive can detect a fatal failure, enter teardown, and teardown then waits for the same automatic keepalive task to finish. That is a self-join; the manual clock only makes the deadlock’s timeout branch permanently visible. I’m tracing the existing “automatic rekey does not wait for fatal teardown” pattern to apply the same ownership rule to keepalive, with regression coverage.
