codex
The fix now mirrors the existing automatic-rekey ownership contract: public keepalive callers still wait for fatal cleanup, while the transport-owned keepalive starts teardown and returns so teardown can safely drain it. I added a real-sshd regression that injects a socket failure into an automatically scheduled keepalive under the manual clock and requires a closed transport with a zero owned-resource snapshot. Formatting and diff checks are clean.
